        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Brrr, it’s snowy out there! Are you "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "ready",
            "ref": "v-ready"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for a snowball fight? Go outside and you may see trucks busy "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " snow and ice. What are they putting on the roads? A lot of road "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "salt",
            "ref": "v-salt"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Road salt is "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "rock salt",
            "zh": "岩盐"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It’s like the table salt you use for food, but not as "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pure",
            "zh": "纯净的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". That’s why it looks brown and "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Why do we put salt on roads? We do this to make roads "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Salt can "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "prevent",
            "zh": "防止"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " water from "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " ice. Pure water becomes ice when it’s 0℃. But if we add salt to water, it won’t turn into ice until it’s about -9℃."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "process",
            "zh": "过程"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " works best when the salt is already "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mixed",
            "ref": "v-mix"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with water before it "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the road. That’s why many cities use a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "mixture",
            "ref": "v-mixture"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of salt and water. And it’s smarter to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " salt before the snow falls!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "在极寒天气里，人们还会往结冰的路面上铺沙子。沙子不能使冰融化，但能降低路面的光滑度，让车辆可以安全行驶。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
